          "convention": "utf8_char_offset",
          "end": 792,
          "source_component_key": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:2.260.030:block:2",
          "start": 624
        },
        "quote": "(c) Terms of office shall be as follows: (1) August 1, 2023, to December 31, 2024; (2) January 1, 2025, to December 31, 2025; (3) January 1, 2026, to December 31, 2026.",
        "ref_id": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:2.260.030:block:2#text",
        "unavailable_reason": null
      },
      {
        "artifact": "normalized_text",
        "availability": "available",
        "label": "TMC 2.260.030 block 3",
        "locator": {
          "block_index": 3,
          "component_id": "89a314de-77e7-58b5-a769-7c8603808aa8",
          "convention": "utf8_char_offset",
          "end": 1230,
          "source_component_key": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:2.260.030:block:3",
          "start": 793
        },
        "quote": "Beginning in 2027, Board members will serve staggered two-year terms. The Mayor shall appoint four Board members to serve from January 1, 2027, to December 31, 2028. These four positions shall be appointed to a two-year term commencing January 1, 2029. Three Board members shall be appointed to serve from January 1, 2027, to December 31, 2027. These three positions shall be appointed to serve two-year terms commencing January 1, 2028.",
        "ref_id": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:2.260.030:block:3#text",
        "unavailable_reason": null
      },
      {
        "artifact": "normalized_text",
        "availability": "available",
        "label": "TMC 2.260.030 block 4",
        "locator": {
          "block_index": 4,
          "component_id": "95a86810-e72e-52a1-8e58-ccbab7da23e7",
          "convention": "utf8_char_offset",
          "end": 1455,
          "source_component_key": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:2.260.030:block:4",
          "start": 1231
        },
        "quote": "Upon expiration of a term the position shall remain vacant until a successor is appointed. Vacancies shall be filled for an unexpired term in the same manner as the original appointments were made. (Ord. 20657 § 2, 5-19-26.)",
